From fe8adfa996c739229bfacadb4b59a63fc9199a23 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 09:20:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 46/53] Harness: a per-task API error or timeout makes that
 task wrong instead of aborting the run (H1)

The dev run C5-S1 died in wave 5: one aiohttp TimeoutError (the API was starved
by a slow worker, ClientSession total=300) in run_loop_now propagated out of
amain and killed the run after 60 of 120 views. BENCHMARK_CONTRACT section 5
says an API error, exception, missing view or timeout is wrong for that task;
the same crash in the single holdout run would consume the shot with no result.

issue.py gets isolating wrappers, and the wave loop in run.py uses only those:
- safe_issue_task: an exception marks the task as an error (Issued.error)
- safe_question_status: a failed poll counts as unresolved, polling goes on
  until the wave deadline
- safe_run_loop_now: logged and counted, the run continues
- safe_collect_view: an exception yields an error view in collect_view's own
  shape ({"task_id", "tenant_id" (the asker's), "status": "error", "error":
  "<ExcType>: <msg[:200]>", "claims": [], ...})
Each failure is logged with the task id (first per kind and task) and counted
in run_manifest.json as api_errors {issue, status, loop, view} plus
api_error_tasks. Exceptions outside the per-task calls (materialize, feed,
worker start) still abort the run. Cancellation is not swallowed.

score.py is unchanged: a status "error" view already yields option None and
reason "error" before the expected-abstain branch, so it scores wrong for every
class (pinned by new tests for ten classes). baseline_central.py already
catches per task and writes an error view, so it is unchanged too.

